\ Module A imports `probe` from module C and defines none of its own; the
\ entry imports a colliding `probe` from module B. A's stored quotation and
\ its undiscovered module word -- both interpreted at runtime inside the
\ image -- must resolve `probe` through A's serialized import edges
\ (Module.deps), deterministically landing on C's export instead of
\ scanning the module cache by name.

use { a-quot: a-call: } "fixtures/own_module_image_deps_a.1z" ;
use { probe: } "fixtures/own_module_image_deps_b.1z" ;

